# host test binaries (test/host/Makefile)
#
# A pattern rather than a list: the list named each binary individually and
# fell six behind as suites were added, leaving compiled executables sitting
# in git status where one could be committed by a wide `git add`.
test/host/test_*
!test/host/test_*.c
!test/host/test_*.h

.DS_Store

# Deleted, and kept ignored so they cannot come back by accident.
#
# These were 197MB of unused local library copies. Neither was built: the
# firmware links LVGL from the registry via lib_deps, and no source file
# includes the audio library at all. Both are re-obtainable -- LVGL is a
# declared dependency and PlatformIO refetches it; the audio library is an
# upstream archive.
#
# lib/lvgl was worse than dead weight. PlatformIO's LDF gives lib/ precedence
# over lib_deps, and that copy was 8.3.10 -- which does not even satisfy the
# `lvgl/lvgl @ ^8.3.11` this project declares, and sat against the 8.4.0 the
# build actually uses. A change in LDF mode would have silently downgraded
# LVGL underneath us, below the floor platformio.ini asks for.
lib/lvgl/
lib/ESP32-audioI2S-master/

# Android companion app (phone/android)
.gradle/
phone/android/build/
phone/android/app/build/
